  "note": "The three High paths through the SHA-pinned `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` revisions were judged overstated: `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` is pinned to a full commit SHA (immutable), and its `curl https://sh.rustup.rs | sh` sits under `if ! command -v rustup`, a guard every hosted image these jobs use satisfies, so the only run-time download is the Rust toolchain from its own distribution: Low at most. Some jobs run on an expression runner (`${{ inputs.runner || 'ubuntu-latest' }}`, `${{ matrix.os }}`) or a third-party label (`blacksmith-*`, whose image the assessment could not read either), where the spec reads the guard as undecidable and the entry as unverified one tier down (section 8.1): once the Windows images are fixed, the case may still wait on that.",
